~ start
if GlobalVariables.haspass == false:
	set GlobalVariables.menutype = "Dialogue"
	 It's a ticket scanner, but the stuff that's corrupting the enviroment is making it all messed up.
	None of the words on the screen are readable, its just a jumbled mess of images and letters. Almost like it's trying to remember how it all goes together, but can't.
		...Seems functional, at least.
	set GlobalVariables.seenreader
	do CutsceneManager.endcutscene()
elif GlobalVariables.haspass == true:
	set GlobalVariables.menumode = "Dialogue"
	I hold my pass up to the scanner, and for a moment the screen...freaks out, like it's not sure what it's supposed to do.
	do sfx_success()
	do get_tree().call_group("breakable_wall", "killwalls")
	...The gate is down, though.
	do CutsceneManager.endcutscene()
=> END